cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AIBA in your research, please cite this software and the associated Master's thesis."
title: "AIBA: Adaptive interval search for efficient hyperparameter tuning"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-11
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Vecino Otero"
    given-names: "José María"
  - family-names: "González Casal"
    given-names: "Alejandro"
  - family-names: "Prieto García"
    given-names: "Abraham"
abstract: >-
  AIBA is an iterative interval-search algorithm that identifies promising
  hyperparameter regions from previously evaluated machine-learning model
  configurations. It is designed to allocate a limited remaining training
  budget more reliably by concentrating new evaluations in regions with strong
  mean performance and low uncertainty.
keywords:
  - hyperparameter optimization
  - surrogate models
  - interval search
  - green artificial intelligence
  - computational efficiency
preferred-citation:
  type: thesis
  title: "Diseño y análisis de modelos subrogados de gemelos digitales para optimización de procesos industriales"
